---
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro'
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'

// The template's own pitch page — linked from the promo band. Explains what
// this site is and the ways an organizer can get one. Plain copy, no magic.
---

<Base
    title='Conference website template — free and open source'
    description='Build a conference website with agenda, speakers, sponsors, tickets, and registration — a free open-source template powered by Cloomba. Self-host it, or we host it for you.'
>
    <PageHeader
        title='Run your conference on this'
        subtitle='Everything you see here is an open-source template with Cloomba as the engine.'
    />
    <article class='mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-8'>
        <div class='prose-content max-w-3xl'>
            <p>
                This entire site — the agenda with its stage filter, the speaker pages, the ticket tiers, coupons, and
                the registration flow — is a static website built from the open-source{' '}
                <strong>Cloomba conference template</strong>. The content comes from a normal Cloomba event; the
                template turns it into a fast site you can host anywhere, under your own domain and brand.
            </p>
            <p>
                Registration, payments, and check-in run on <a href='https://cloomba.com' rel='noopener'>Cloomba</a>, an
                EU-hosted event platform: attendees register in the embedded widget, get QR tickets and wallet passes,
                and your team checks them in with the Cloomba app at the door. Your site never touches payments or
                personal data.
            </p>

            <h2>Your options</h2>
            <p><strong>1. Self-host this template — free.</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Create your event on <a href='https://cloomba.com' rel='noopener'>cloomba.com</a> — agenda, speakers,
                    sponsors, ticket tiers, coupons, registration questions.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Get a free read-only API key under <a href='https://cloomba.com/me/developers' rel='noopener'
                        >Developers</a
                    >.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Clone <a href='https://github.com/cloomba/conference-template' rel='noopener'>the template</a>, put
                    your event's slug and your colors in <code>site.config.ts</code>, and deploy the static build to any
                    host.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Free events cost nothing at all; for paid tickets Cloomba keeps a small platform fee — the site itself
                never adds a cent.
            </p>

            <p><strong>2. Just use your Cloomba event page.</strong></p>
            <p>
                Every Cloomba event already has a full public page with registration, agenda, and a photo wall — no
                website project needed. The template is for when you want your own domain and a conference-shaped site
                around it.
            </p>

            <p><strong>3. Cloomba Cloud.</strong></p>
            <p>
                The same site, hosted for you: set your colors, connect your domain — no repository, no build step.{' '}
                <a href='https://cloomba.com/info/contact' rel='noopener'>Contact us</a> and we'll set you up.
            </p>

            <h2>Documentation</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <a href='/cloomba-for-conferences/features'>Features</a> — everything this site demonstrates, itemized.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href='/cloomba-for-conferences/configuration'>Configuration</a> — every option in <code
                        >site.config.ts</code
                    >, explained.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href='/cloomba-for-conferences/customization'>Customization</a> — content files, colors, imagery, adding
                    sections.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href='/cloomba-for-conferences/deployment'>Deployment</a> — build and host anywhere; keeping the site
                    fresh.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Questions</h2>
            <p>
                Use the <a href='https://cloomba.com/info/contact' rel='noopener'>Cloomba contact form</a> — or open an issue
                on{' '}
                <a href='https://github.com/cloomba/conference-template' rel='noopener'>GitHub</a> if it's about the template
                itself.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</Base>
